00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:22.060
Dividend investing in Canada focuses on companies that return cash to shareholders through regular

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.060
payments that often grow over time.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:29.760
Forda stands out because it operates regulated utilities that generate stable revenue from

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:32.740
essential services like electricity and natural gas.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:38.880
The company reported earnings of 78 cents per share in its most recent quarter, two cents

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:40.200
better than the prior year.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:47.200
Its dividend yield sits at 3.4%, and the streak of annual increases now totals 52 years.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:54.180
Investors can implement this by allocating TFSA room to Fortis shares and re-investing dividends

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.840
through a DRIP program offered by most Canadian brokers.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:03.920
This approach performed well during the 2008 financial crisis, when many growth stocks

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.040
fell sharply while utilities held up.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:11.800
The main risk is rising interest rates that can pressure valuation multiples on income stocks.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:17.180
Fortis also serves parts of the United States and the Caribbean, spreading its regular

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:19.660
regulatory protections across multiple jurisdictions.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:23.440
The business model relies on long-term rate frameworks

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:25.480
that allow predictable cost recovery

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:27.780
and returns on infrastructure investments.

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:30.820
Canadian investors often pair this holding

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:32.880
with similar names like TC Energy

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:36.320
to balance pipeline exposure against pure regulated

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.520
utility cash flows.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.460
Imagine you check your CRA account

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:43.220
and see a contribution room figure that looks current.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:45.320
The actual number may lag

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:51.840
because the agency updates TFSA data only once a year based on the previous calendar year's transactions.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:03:00.140
For 2026, the base annual limit is $7,000, but your personal room could be higher from unused amounts

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:02.460
or withdrawals made in 2025.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:09.120
Using an outdated figure risks an over-contribution penalty of 1% per month on the excess.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:14.280
The pro tip is to keep your own spreadsheet of every contribution and withdrawal date,

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:18.460
so you always know the precise room available before you fund the account.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:24.680
Most retail investors assume the CRA portal is live when it is not, and the simple fix

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.760
is to cross-reference your own records before every deposit.

